meta {
  name: Create Static Product List
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Static List",
    "type": "Static"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.type: eq Static
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4`, for Channels/Ecatalogs (Phase
  4) to reference via `product_list_id`.

  `201 Created`.

  ## Major finding -- how "Static" list membership actually works
  Neither `ProductListCreateInputDto` nor the create response has any
  field for a fixed member-ID array (`product_ids` etc. don't exist).
  Instead, creating a `type: "Static"` list **auto-generates a `query`**
  targeting the list's own id:
  `[[{"operator":"in","field":"static_lists","value":["<this list's own
  id>"],"field_type":"PimProductAttribute.ObjectIdAttribute"}]]`. So a
  Static list is really just a Smart list whose query is
  `static_lists contains <list_id>` -- membership isn't stored on the
  list at all, it's stored on **each product's own `static_list_ids`
  field**. To add a product to this list, `PATCH /products/{id}` with
  `{"static_list_ids": ["6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4"]}` -- confirmed working
  (see `02-Products-v3`'s kept product, which now has this list linked;
  verify via `GET /products/{id}/static_lists`, a computed subpath, not
  via `_fields=static_list_ids` on the main resource, which is silently
  dropped like other relationship-array fields in this API).

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  List names are unique per account. Re-running once the fixture exists
  returns `422 {"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"A
  List with same name already exists"}]}` -- expected, not a bug
  (`config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #38a).
}
